istic knowledge by emphasizing how an applicant's savings relative to the credit duration could influence their ability to repay the loan in a timely manner. For example, higher savings coupled with similar durations could infer stronger creditworthiness.\n\n# Convert savings_status into ordinal values\nsavings_status_mapping = {'<100': 1, 'no known savings': 2, '100<=X<500': 3, '500<=X<1000': 4, '>=1000': 5}\ndf['savings_status_ordinal'] = df['savings_status'].map(savings_status_mapping)\n\n# Calculate the interaction ratio feature\ndf['interaction_savings_status_duration_ratio'] = df['savings_status_ordinal'] / df['duration_bins'].replace({'short-term': 1, 'mid-term': 2, 'long-term': 3})\n```end\n\n```python\n# Feature name: employment_effective_years_bin\n# Feature description: Bin employment_effective_years into discrete categories (e.g., short, medium, long) using quantiles for distinguishing different asset building periods that might show creditworthiness trends.\n# Usefulness: Creditworthiness patterns based on employment tenure can be better captured in buckets rather than individual years, simplifying the relationship for models to learn while retaining interpretability. For example, shorter employment years might correlate with less financial stability.\n\n# Using quantiles to bin employment_effective_years\nemployment_bins_labels = ['short', 'medium', 'long']\ndf['employment_effective_years_bin'] = pd.qcut(df['employment_effective_years'], q=3, labels=employment_bins_labels)\n```end\n\n```python\n# Feature name: age_credit_history_interaction_score\n# Feature description: Create a feature that combines age and credit_history_delinquency_score by calculating their product, which captures the interaction between the applicant's age and their delinquency score.\n# Usefulness: Older individuals with lower credit history delinquency scores (indicating good credit history) are likely to exhibit better repayment behavior. This feature emphasizes the interaction